# Strapi Cloud production — durable S3 images (not ephemeral `/uploads/`)

## Production policy (mandatory)

- **Production Cloud images must be durable on S3.** Do **not** use ephemeral Cloud `/uploads/` (migration base64 / `finish:collection-images-on-cloud`) as the production path.
- Strapi Cloud **disk is ephemeral**. A Strapi **release/redeploy** deletes files under `/uploads/` even when DB `image` / `cover` relations still point at them → live site shows placeholders; `HEAD` returns **404**.
- **After any Strapi Cloud deploy**, verify production media URLs are `https://…amazonaws.com/…` (or the configured S3 host). If they are `/uploads/…`, re-run the **S3** push — not the ephemeral finish script.
- Frontend (`mosc-temp`) resolves relative URLs via `NEXT_PUBLIC_STRAPI_URL` + `getMediaUrl` — fix Cloud/S3 files, not the Next app.

```bash
# ✅ DO — durable production default
npm run push:collection-images-s3-to-cloud -- --collection=institutions --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2 --skip-api

# ❌ DON'T — ephemeral (wiped on next Cloud deploy)
npm run finish:collection-images-on-cloud -- --collection=institutions --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
```

**Verified (Jul 2026):** Institutions for `mosc_malankara_orthodox_2` looked fine after ephemeral finish, then broke after a Strapi release deploy. S3 register fixed **219/219** with `HEAD 200` on `eventapp-media-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com`.

## When images are missing on production

- Content/tenant links exist on Cloud, but cards show placeholders or broken images.
- API `populate=image` (or `cover`) returns a URL, but `HEAD` is **404**.
- Symptom of ephemeral path: `image.url` like `/uploads/ca_….jpeg` (relative) instead of S3.
- Local `http://localhost:3000/...` can still look fine — local `public/uploads/` is unaffected by Cloud redeploy.

## Production vs demo tenant (critical)

| Audience | Tenant ID |
|---|---|
| Live site (`www.mosc-temp.com`, Amplify) | **`mosc_malankara_orthodox_2`** |
| Editor / demo CMS | `tenant_demo_002` |

Always pass `--tenant-id=` explicitly. In [scripts/lib/liturgy-cli.js](mdc:scripts/lib/liturgy-cli.js), **CLI flags override `.env` `TENANT_ID`** — confirm the log line `Tenant: mosc_malankara_orthodox_2` before trusting the run.

