## Two upload strategies

### A — Durable (S3 + register-s3-media) — **default for production**

Use for any production / live-tenant image fix. Survives Strapi Cloud redeploys.

```bash
# Stop local Strapi first (script embeds Strapi to read local DB).
# Requires .env: STRAPI_CLOUD_URL, STRAPI_CLOUD_API_TOKEN, AWS_*
npm run push:collection-images-s3-to-cloud -- --collection=institutions --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2 --skip-api
# optional flags: --skip-s3 | --link-existing | omit --skip-api to try Cloud /api/upload first
npm run push:all-collection-images-s3-to-cloud -- --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
```

- Needs local `.env` AWS creds (`AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, `AWS_REGION`, `AWS_S3_BUCKET_NAME`) writing to shared prod prefix (`S3_UPLOAD_PREFIX`, default `strapi-editorial-media/prod`).
- Prefer Node matching local `better-sqlite3` (often Node 22 on this machine) if default shell Node breaks native modules.
- ACL: omit when bucket is “Bucket owner enforced” — [strapi-aws-s3-upload-omit-acl-when-bucket-owner-enforced.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/strapi-aws-s3-upload-omit-acl-when-bucket-owner-enforced.mdc).
- Details: [STRAPI_MEDIA_STORAGE_S3_CLOUD_PRD.html](mdc:documentation/STRAPI_MEDIA_STORAGE_S3_CLOUD_PRD.html).

**Success criteria:** every `image.url` (or `cover` / `cardImage` / `pdf` / `media`) is an **S3 absolute URL** and `HEAD` returns **200**.

### B — Ephemeral quick fix (migration base64 → Cloud local disk) — **emergency only**

Use **only** when S3/AWS is unavailable and you need a temporary unblock. Expect images to **break again on the next Cloud deploy**.

```bash
npm run finish:collection-images-on-cloud -- --collection=institutions --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
# Batch (still ephemeral):
npm run finish:all-collection-images-on-cloud -- --tenant-id=mosc_malankara_orthodox_2
```

- Success log looks like: `Created: 9 | Linked: 219`
- Windows may exit non-zero with `UV_HANDLE_CLOSING` after success — treat **Created/Linked** as the result.
- **Must** follow up with strategy A (S3) before considering production done.
- Agent must **warn** the user that this will not survive redeploy.

